    docs={
      'JEV_PHASE13_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC.md':'# Stage2 architecture freeze\n\nInput is VFCE1024, current detection metadata8, per-ID metadata12, pair evidence16, four historical1024 tokens (recent, native Gallery mean, current-view mean, other-view mean). Global ID integers remain outside the network. Arbitrary D/K are padded and masked; each detection has a private terminal.\n\n256D projection; eight shared state latents read the current detections and legal bank, followed by two latent self-attention layers. A real question contains six evidence keys: current visual/task, current metadata, pooled global history, current-view summary, other-view summary, pooled legal pair evidence. Question evidence self-attention and state reading precede each option reading all six question keys and shared state. Mean/max legal-option context adds explicit competition. Dynamic tanh question gate modulates the option residual. Separate MATCH and REACT heads score legal identities and DEFER/START_NEW; masked outputs go to native capacity-one Hungarian with private terminals. No single-key QuestionReader.\n\nFull registered parameters: 4,230,659. Style controls: 4,099,075 (3.1% fewer). Actual executed matrix multiply profiles use real shapes, not dormant parameter count. Ablations may retain dormant reader parameters; removed compute and gradients are disclosed. MEMORY WRITE/KEEP head is untrained and never writes; REACT formal support is insufficient and uses the common .75 cosine terminal fallback.\n\nNo-cross removes other-view appearance/global observation counts and timestamps from tensors while retaining the frozen legal global namespace. No-long removes prototype/view-summary visual tokens and recomputes all similarity evidence. The same transform executes in collate and native input building. No-competition removes only explicit mean/max context; causal question/state context remains. No-typed-head is diagnostic under MATCH-only supervision: typed lifecycle value cannot be identified.\n',
      'JEV_PHASE13_GMT_STAGE2_CONTRACT.md':'# Native global identity contract\n\nOnly JEV_DIRECT replaces original GTA scoring. OFF follows the original code branches. SHADOW discards independent logits and cannot change original assignments. The real direct executor operates on actual Instances, shared ordered native Gallery, hit counters, possible IDs and old-ReID bank. Frame0 initializes the camera with most detections; later payloads follow native camera order. Historical observations span the native40-frame window. All actual legal active IDs are candidates; no GTA retrieval scores. The bank uses original eligibility>=10 observations/promotion/prototype rules.\n\nMATCH existing-ID or DEFER is followed by an actual stale query for unmatched rows. REACT existing stale-ID or START_NEW has a separate terminal meaning. Capacity-one Hungarian enforces unique ID within one camera; cameras can share IDs. Each actual birth/restore/association causes exactly one original native write. No trained MEMORY head is enabled without WRITE/KEEP labels. Identity metadata updates only after the committed observation, before the next decision.\n\nLossless prefixes include original Instances/Gallery alias graph, hits, bank, ID counter, explicit trajectory RNG, global RNG and `phase13_identity_meta`. Missing metadata is forbidden for DIRECT resumes. The GTA/RPCE/activated pipeline throws in the full engineering lifecycle test. Test logits are forced after a real NN forward only to cover legal lifecycle branches; they are not tracking or training evidence. Original221 OFF/SHADOW prefix+next-frame traces are exact.\n',
      'JEV_PHASE13_TRAINING_PROTOCOL.md':'# Frozen learning protocol\n\nRead reports/JEV_PHASE13/TRAINING_PROTOCOL.json for exact hashes, seeds, Tiny selection and gates. Smoke/invariants and real GTA-free/native lifecycle pass first. Tiny1000, Pilot1000, then each method receives a fresh common20,000 AdamW updates, batch4 full natural camera payload groups, LR1e-4, weight decay.01, clip1, FP32. Seeds20261008/09/10. No Tiny/Pilot weights initialize formal models.\n\nLabels are partial: multi-positive certified-option CE, .25 structured loss-augmented capacity-one assignment margin, .1 Brier. UNKNOWN candidates never become negatives; calibration is conditional on certified choices. Development groups at every32nd frame form the frozen audit/calibration subset; HOTA cannot select checkpoints or hyperparameters. Primary checkpoint is LAST at common20k; BEST is diagnostic. Formal tasks are MATCH only; REACT .75 cosine and native MEMORY WRITE fallbacks are identical across all methods.\n\nTiny includes later ordinary states from each TRAIN video, cross-camera, competition, hard positive, real stale and real scene-new/empty candidate groups selected solely by labels before optimization. Tiny recovery memorization cannot qualify the rare REACT task for formal learning.\n\nAfter normal association is learned, at most one own-state TRAIN rollout/relabel/4k fine-tune round is allowed. All main style baselines receive their own same-sized round; comparison at total24k is separate from20k. Contamination remains UNKNOWN. Three-task lifecycle and heldout remain NOT_RUN until support/science gates qualify; inherited feature-pretraining exposure prevents independent heldout authorization.\n',
      'JEV_PHASE13_FAIR_BASELINES.md':'# Controlled baseline comparison\n\nB0 is the original strong Stage2-trained GMT full system. It uses different Stage2-transferred visual/RPCE features and is reported separately, never as a same-frontend association ablation. B1 max cosine over recent/native prototype/current-view history with fixed .75 private terminal. B2 historical trajectory-conditioned dynamic pointer decoder, B3 dense candidate/detection association, B4 candidate Set Attention, B5 state/question/option/gated typed JEV.\n\nB2/B3 are explicit MOTIP-style/CAMEL-style controlled adapters, not complete official MOTIP/CAMELTrack reproductions. They share the same frozen Stage1, causal memory tensors, legal pools, native solver/fallbacks, partial GT labels and optimizer budget. They replace Full question/option readers/gate with four ordinary attention readers. MOTIP-style uses three state cross-readers then current six-evidence context; CAMEL-style uses two candidate self-readers and two state readers; Set uses three candidate self-readers and one shared-state cross-reader. Their actual shared-state encoder participates in the decision and receives nonzero supervised gradients as a controlled common frontend for association; official papers differ in detector/query/ID-slot design.\n\nFull4.231M versus controls4.099M registered parameters is a3.1% difference, within frozen10% capacity tolerance. Actual executed MAC and dormant ablation modules are disclosed. All twelve variants and three seeds receive the same20k update budget and all three fixed complete development videos. No favorable sequence selection. No typed/calibration advantage can be claimed where only MATCH is qualified or positive uniform temperature leaves assignment unchanged.\n'
    }
